# Cursor + NassAI-Praxis

- Always load NassAI-Praxis before coding.
- Read `praxis.config.md`, `memory/semantic/conventions.md`, and `memory/working/current.md`.
- Check `skills/` before implementing any feature.
- Use PascalCase for components/classes, camelCase for application variables/functions, snake_case for database fields, and kebab-case for files.
- Keep repositories responsible for data access, services responsible for business logic, and controllers responsible for HTTP concerns.
- Before writing memory, scan against `memory/security/deny-list.md` and classify the content.
- When `.cursorrules` conflicts with `memory/semantic/conventions.md`, Praxis wins; resolve the conflict explicitly and log it.
